WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.260
Germany, December 1935.

2
00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:07.670
A Berlin woman named Regina
Jonas is ordained as a rabbi.

3
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.430
Her thesis had asked whether a woman could
hold rabbinic office under Jewish law.

4
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.210
She argued yes.

5
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:17.980
In 1942 she was deported
to Theresienstadt.

6
00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:21.490
In 1944 she was murdered at Auschwitz.

7
00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:25.840
The next woman rabbi was
not ordained until 1972.

8
00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.690
Why did it take so long?

9
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:31.340
In this mission, you'll trace women
rabbis from Berlin to Britain,

10
00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:34.780
America and beyond, movement by movement.

11
00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:39.340
Then you'll weigh up the debate: is
ordaining women a development of Judaism,

12
00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:40.850
or a break with it?

13
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:46.370
Your mission: find out why it took
until 1972 for another woman rabbi.
